cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "exotic-ccr-lean: Lean 4 Gate-0 certificates for the EXOTIC-CCR Jacobian counterexample anchor"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fredriksen
    given-names: Daniel Eric
    affiliation: "Quantyra Inc"
url: "https://github.com/Quantyra/exotic-ccr-lean"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Quantyra/exotic-ccr-lean"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Jacobian conjecture
  - multivariate polynomials
  - formal verification
  - EXOTIC-CCR
  - Quantyra
abstract: >-
  Machine-checked Lean 4 certificates for Gate 0 of Project EXOTIC-CCR:
  Jacobian determinant det DF = -2, three-point collision identities, and
  standard non-injectivity packaging for the announced polynomial map F
  (and det-1 form G), the full algebraic cotangent-lift Theorem B including
  canonical Poisson generator brackets, real-vector-field incompleteness,
  canonical minimal transport core, and a deficiency-to-not-ESS operator
  bridge. At the untagged, unreleased commit
  a6bb091c05943cfcf35c405659e57df93ab8bb3d, the named theorem
  ExoticCCR.theoremE proves that the canonical minimal X1 transport core is
  not essentially self-adjoint. Deficiency-index values and full Theorem F
  remain historical paper-only results and are not Lean-covered. No result for
  arbitrary transport realizations, preferred extension, extension count,
  strong CCR/Weyl, C-star, CP, channels, gates, physical significance, or
  computational advantage is claimed. No release version, release tag,
  version DOI, or Zenodo DOI exists for this new theorem freeze.
